# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: framed on Safari, someone presses ⌘N. The new window floats over the framed one. They look at the
# neighbouring window and come back: the new window is still there. (F57; before, it was gone and Back did
# not bring it back.)
# Reference: T34 T52.
open Safari
open Notes
arrange
zoom 101
open Safari 500x400
expect floating 103
expect visible 103
expect camera 101
neighbor right
expect hidden 103
back
expect camera 101
expect visible 103
# With everything in view it sits on the Desktop like any floating window.
show-all
expect visible 103
expect left-of 102 103
# ⌘Tab to it from somewhere else frames the window it belongs to.
zoom 102
expect hidden 103
flush
focus 103
expect camera 101
expect visible 103
# Closing its host makes it an ordinary floating window.
close 101
flush
desktop
expect visible 103
